robot-sport (0.1.7-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * feat(adapter_lynx): support mode-aware velocity dispatch (normalized
    Command=21 in regular mode, absolute Command=25 in navigation mode) while
    keeping ROS cmd_vel in SI units; expose regular/navigation mode, RL
    control, and standard/agile flat/stairs gait actions through ROS2 and the
    HTTP motion API, with gait transitions serializing mode/RL prep, a
    zero-velocity send, and BasicStatus confirmation.
  * fix(adapter_lynx): reject stale, non-finite, unsupported, or unsafe control
    states; keep legacy walk as a standard-flat alias and reject undefined trot
    gait 4098 without sending it to the robot.
  * feat: add motions[].display_name to MotionDescriptor (id fallback when
    empty) and mirror it in the robot_switch_server motion cache, so
    /system_info always reports a non-empty label for all 16 in-tree motions
    (lynx 10, go2 4, fake 2).
  * chore(robot_switch_server): increase the default motion RPC timeout to 6000
    ms for confirmed mode, RL-state, and gait transition sequences.
  * test: cover Lynx Command=21/25 payloads, SI limiting, and the
    navigation-to-RL-to-agile-gait confirmation sequence; add
    robot_adapter_interfaces' first gtest target for the display_name fallback
    and struct field ordering.
  * docs: document one-call agile gait control, mode-specific velocity units,
    transition constraints, configuration, failure behavior, and
    motions[].display_name across the /system_info and /motion API docs and
    the adapter developer guide.

 -- robot-sport <gs-dev@example.com>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:57:51 +0800

